": "nervous and unable to relax", "examples": ["Everyone was on edge waiting for the results."]}, {"id": "ac099", "head": "pleasantly surprised", "pos": "adv + adj", "meaning": "surprised because something is better than you expected", "examples": ["I was pleasantly surprised by how cheap the hotel was."]}, {"id": "ac100", "head": "a pang of guilt", "pos": "noun + prep + noun", "meaning": "a sudden, short feeling of guilt", "examples": ["I felt a pang of guilt when I saw her waiting alone."]}, {"id": "ac101", "head": "fly off the handle", "pos": "idiom", "meaning": "to suddenly become very angry", "examples": ["He flies off the handle at the smallest thing."]}, {"id": "ac102", "head": "over the moon", "pos": "idiom", "meaning": "extremely happy", "examples": ["She was over the moon when she got the job."]}, {"id": "ac103", "head": "come to terms with", "pos": "phrase", "meaning": "to slowly accept something sad or difficult", "examples": ["It took him years to come to terms with his father's death."]}, {"id": "ac104", "head": "a mixed reaction", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "a response in which some people like something and others don't", "examples": ["The film received a mixed reaction from critics."]}, {"id": "ac105", "head": "not bat an eyelid", "pos": "idiom", "meaning": "to show no surprise or worry at all", "examples": ["She didn't bat an eyelid when they told her the price."]}]}, {"id": "act8", "title": "Work and business", "words": [{"id": "ac106", "head": "launch a product", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to start selling a new product", "examples": ["The company will launch its new product in the spring."]}, {"id": "ac107", "head": "a gap in the market", "pos": "noun + prep + noun", "meaning": "a chance to sell something that nobody else sells yet", "examples": ["They spotted a gap in the market for healthy vegan snacks."]}, {"id": "ac108", "head": "go out of business", "pos": "phrase", "meaning": "(of a company) to stop trading because it has failed", "examples": ["Many small shops went out of business during the crisis."]}, {"id": "ac109", "head": "cut costs", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to reduce the amount of money spent", "examples": ["The firm cut costs by moving its office outside the city."]}, {"id": "ac110", "head": "a lucrative deal", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "an agreement that makes a lot of money", "examples": ["They signed a lucrative deal with a Japanese company."]}, {"id": "ac111", "head": "corner the market", "pos": "idiom", "meaning": "to control most of the sales of a particular product", "examples": ["One company has cornered the market in online search."]}, {"id": "ac112", "head": "make a profit", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to earn more money than you spend", "examples": ["The café made a profit in its first year."]}, {"id": "ac113", "head": "a cut-throat industry", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "a business area where competition is very fierce", "examples": ["Fashion is a cut-throat industry."]}, {"id": "ac114", "head": "climb the career ladder", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to get better and better jobs within a profession", "examples": ["She climbed the career ladder quickly and became a director at 35."]}, {"id": "ac115", "head": "strike a deal", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to reach an agreement, especially in business", "examples": ["The two firms struck a deal after months of talks."]}, {"id": "ac116", "head": "a steady income", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "money that you earn regularly", "examples": ["Freelancers often lack a steady income."]}, {"id": "ac117", "head": "run a business", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to own and manage a company", "examples": ["He has run his own business since he was twenty-five."]}, {"id": "ac118", "head": "hand in your notice", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to tell your employer formally that you are leaving your job", "examples": ["She handed in her notice after a row with her manager."]}, {"id": "ac119", "head": "job satisfaction", "pos": "noun + noun", "meaning": "the feeling of pleasure you get from your work", "examples": ["Many teachers say job satisfaction matters more than pay."]}, {"id": "ac120", "head": "a heavy workload", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "a large amount of work that you have to do", "examples": ["Nurses often complain about a heavy workload."]}]}, {"id": "act9", "title": "Society and the public", "words": [{"id": "ac121", "head": "public opinion", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "what most people in a society think about something", "examples": ["Public opinion has turned against the new airport."]}, {"id": "ac122", "head": "raise awareness", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to make more people know about a problem", "examples": ["The campaign aims to raise awareness of mental health."]}, {"id": "ac123", "head": "a growing concern", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "a problem that more and more people worry about", "examples": ["Loneliness among older people is a growing concern."]}, {"id": "ac124", "head": "widen the gap", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to increase the difference between two groups", "examples": ["Critics say the reform will widen the gap between rich and poor."]}, {"id": "ac125", "head": "play a key role", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to be very important in an activity or situation", "examples": ["Volunteers play a key role in the local community."]}, {"id": "ac126", "head": "far-reaching consequences", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "results that affect a lot of people or things", "examples": ["The decision will have far-reaching consequences for farmers."]}, {"id": "ac127", "head": "take measures", "pos": "verb + noun", "meaning": "to do things officially to deal with a problem", "examples": ["The government must take measures to reduce traffic."]}, {"id": "ac128", "head": "a vested interest", "pos": "adj + noun", "meaning": "a personal reason for wanting something to happen, usually because you will gain from